1
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:05,640
What would your daily schedule as a child in Thanh Cong look like?

2
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:05,940
What did you do?

3
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,379
How did you experience your childhood life back then?

4
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:14,080
When I think about my childhood here, I think specifically of when I was in elementary school.

5
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:14,380
Yeah.

6
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,480
When I was in elementary school,

7
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:17,880
the Thanh Cong area

8
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:19,920
in my memories was—

9
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:22,760
I think it revolved around three main locations.

10
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:25,280
In the morning, I had to go to school,

11
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:28,220
so I would be dropped off in Thanh Cong

12
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,780
on my mom's or dad's motorbike.

13
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:35,240
Because I was usually half-sleepy then, the first thing I would remember was the school gate.

14
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:35,640
Yeah.

15
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:41,100
Now, Thanh Cong A Elementary School has been rebuilt, and the old school gate was very different.

16
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:41,520
It was very different.

17
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:44,260
The old Thanh Cong school gate was lower,

18
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:49,920
and there weren't many vehicles going in and out of the old school.

19
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:52,980
More people walked to school back then, so there weren't motorbikes parked

20
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:56,699
in massive crowds at the gate like there are now.

21
00:00:58,340 --> 00:00:58,680
Ah,

22
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:04,700
back then, when I thought about the old school gate, the sounds that came to mind were

23
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:08,680
usually the security guard's voice, greetings,

24
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:12,020
parents saying goodbye to kids and kids saying goodbye to parents.

25
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:13,190
And then,

26
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:15,500
the sound of the school drum.

27
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:21,200
The school drum sound brought back a lot of feelings,

28
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,680
especially the feeling of panic and fear of being late.

29
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:25,899
Yeah.

30
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,760
Particularly when I was lingering outside the gate eating snacks.

31
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:32,760
Back then, there were two things I loved doing at the school gate.

32
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:34,140
Those were

33
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:40,300
buying toys and collectibles, like soccer player cards or Vinamilk cards

34
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:46,260
to collect in a folder. Back then, I always felt that

35
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:50,940
a kid's "status" and "wealth" was determined by whether they had more cards than their peers.

36
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:53,240
So we were always trying to keep up with the trend.

37
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:59,500
- Do you still keep those cards?
- I think if I search, I'll find them.

38
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:01,920
[laughs] They are probably in the third floor storage space,

39
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:03,820
right near the old chaise longue.

40
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:05,360
- Go on.
- Right.

41
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:10,519
The second thing I really loved at the school gate was

42
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:16,520
a comic book rental shop. Back then, buying comic books to read was very expensive.

43
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:22,660
And when I first learned how to read, I felt like since I had this ability, I had to utilize it.

44
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:25,580
[laughs] And my parents strongly supported it

45
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:25,900
because

46
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:30,020
it trained my reading habits and language skills.

47
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:32,740
So I often rented Doraemon

48
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:34,540
and Greek mythology books.

49
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:36,340
Ah,

50
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:40,420
renting them cost about two thousand or three thousand VND a day.

51
00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:45,080
By the time I went to school, those rental shops were gone. Around when did they disappear?

52
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:47,680
- I think I rented them until the end of elementary school, so maybe—

53
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:48,300
Yeah.

54
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:52,620
- End of elementary school?
- Or end of fourth grade, around that time.

55
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:56,420
That was when I stopped caring about rented comic books, and started buying them instead.

56
00:02:56,420 --> 00:03:01,260
The price of comic books started dropping very quickly.

57
00:03:01,260 --> 00:03:04,740
Or maybe our family got wealthier, I don't know. Or people could afford to pay more for comic books.

58
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:09,220
Naturally, the "funnel" was that people would read them at the rental shops first before deciding to buy.

60
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:15,480
Oh, but how do you feel about the fact that they disappeared by fourth grade?

61
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:20,500
From your first to fourth grade, how was Hanoi that people had to rent comic books?

62
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:23,440
Whereas by the time I entered first grade, that experience was completely gone.

64
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:27,620
I think it depended.

65
00:03:28,970 --> 00:03:31,480
I don't think every school gate had a comic book rental shop.

66
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:31,920
Firstly,

67
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:34,740
maybe it was unique to...

68
00:03:35,410 --> 00:03:38,820
I couldn't find any other rental shop other than the one at our school gate.

69
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:41,360
- It was an old culture of Hanoi.
- Oh.

71
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:45,680
But I still don't understand why it existed in your time but not in mine.

72
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:47,500
- We are only four years apart.
- Yeah.

73
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:54,460
I think by the time I was in fifth grade, buying comic books at bookstores was already quite easy.

74
00:03:54,460 --> 00:03:55,340
Yeah.

75
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:59,000
But back then... I think...

76
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:05,340
I don't know. Many of those rental shops were very small,

77
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:05,580
they only had

78
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:07,780
about

79
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:10,560
a few hundred books.

80
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:15,260
But back then, Doraemon had many short stories, and you read them very quickly.

81
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:19,019
I'd read them under my desk at school in two days, and then I'd have to rent new ones.

82
00:04:19,019 --> 00:04:21,399
- OK.
- So buying them would have been very expensive and inefficient.

83
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:22,660
- Yeah, makes sense.
- Sharing economy.

84
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:25,460
The first sharing economy model I knew before Grab.

85
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:29,680
- OK [laughs].
- OK.

87
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:31,450
OK [laughs].

88
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:33,650
- Where were we?
- Yes, at the school gate.

89
00:04:33,650 --> 00:04:36,610
Those were the two things I liked at the school gate. Did you like eating snacks?

90
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:37,980
I

91
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:42,300
liked snacks but I mostly just wanted to follow the trends. I wanted to try them,

92
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:44,820
but I actually didn't like eating most of them. Back then, there was this lipstick candy.

93
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:47,280
I didn't have that in my time. You have to tell me about it.

94
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:48,110
Lipstick candy was

95
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:51,820
a candy shaped like a tube of lipstick. It made us feel very grown-up.

96
00:04:51,820 --> 00:04:52,590
- Ah, I remember now.
- You twist it up and then—

97
00:04:52,590 --> 00:04:54,620
- Kids don't have that anymore.
- You apply it on your lips and lick it.

98
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:56,620
- Yeah, I remember. I think you bought that for me once.
- It was full of chemical colorings.

99
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:58,750
And back then, in front of the school gate,

100
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:06,580
there were shops selling yo-yos and other toys.

101
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:09,840
- Yeah, yo-yos.
- Yes, yo-yos [laughs]. OK.

102
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:15,320
Yes, there were three toys that we often bought back then. First was the yo-yo,

103
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:18,750
- second was the spinning top.
- Yes.

104
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:22,320
And third was Bakugan. You throw them and they transform.

105
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:25,200
No, I don't know that one. I only know about the spinning tops.

106
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:29,760
In general, the animation industry heavily dictated children's toys back then.

107
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:29,960
Yeah.

108
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:31,560
Those Chinese shows that broadcasted on VTV.

109
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:34,400
- Right.
- What about now?

110
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:36,860
- Like Fruity Robo and stuff.
- But now they don't buy that anymore.

111
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:39,710
- I think they still do, but now they buy character merch.
- Yeah.

112
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:42,159
- Like keychains on backpacks.
- But that's for grown-ups like us. Kids like Bean,

113
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:42,960
they don't play those games anymore. They buy Skibidi Toilet toys.

114
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:45,500
- They still buy them, but—
- Yeah, it's still the same concept.

115
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:49,000
I don't really know what kids play nowadays.

116
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,720
- Yeah.
- OK, go on.

117
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:55,320
What other things do you remember?

118
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:58,490
Food-wise, the best food that I loved the most was lime popsicles.

119
00:05:58,490 --> 00:05:59,400
I think it was because we didn't have air conditioning at school.

120
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:02,200
- Oh, OK.
- So lime popsicles were even more satisfying.

121
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:07,100
- Yeah. You experienced going to school without air conditioning, but I never had to.
- We only got air conditioners when I was in third or fourth grade.

122
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:12,671
So by your time, they didn't sell lime popsicles anymore.

123
00:06:12,672 --> 00:06:15,692
- Yeah.
- Supply and demand.

124
00:06:15,692 --> 00:06:17,852
Also, when there was no air conditioning, we could hear all the sounds outside.

125
00:06:17,852 --> 00:06:19,992
In class, you'd hear birds chirping and lessons from the adjacent classroom.

126
00:06:19,992 --> 00:06:22,611
- Because the windows and doors were open.
- Teachers would often argue if one class was too loud.

127
00:06:22,612 --> 00:06:25,992
- Ah.
- Now that doors are kept closed, it's much better.

128
00:06:25,992 --> 00:06:28,652
Yeah.

129
00:06:28,652 --> 00:06:28,712
So that's food and toys.

130
00:06:28,712 --> 00:06:33,312
What about school-related memories?

131
00:06:33,312 --> 00:06:36,292
Okay. After school, did your grandparents pick you up at the gate?

132
00:06:36,292 --> 00:06:36,552
Well,

133
00:06:37,212 --> 00:06:39,092
dismissal time was always very noisy.

134
00:06:39,092 --> 00:06:43,312
Kids would run around the schoolyard before going home.

135
00:06:43,312 --> 00:06:45,192
But I usually went straight home because I had something more exciting waiting: video games.

136
00:06:45,192 --> 00:06:48,362
I was always eager to get home and play games.

137
00:06:48,362 --> 00:06:48,712
[laughs] I mean, our family ran an internet cafe, so it was an awesome childhood.

138
00:06:50,132 --> 00:06:54,552
- Yeah.
- Besides ours, there were many other internet cafes around the school.

139
00:06:54,552 --> 00:06:59,772
But ours was quite large and had a lot of customers since it was the closest one.

140
00:07:00,632 --> 00:07:00,872
Yeah.

141
00:07:01,792 --> 00:07:03,252
Back then, when my grandmother ran it,

142
00:07:04,772 --> 00:07:08,572
a full setup included a bulky CRT monitor, a mouse, keyboard, headphones, and a webcam.

143
00:07:08,572 --> 00:07:12,472
- Yes. And those computers had a huge box unit behind them.
- A huge CPU unit.

144
00:07:12,472 --> 00:07:15,472
Exactly. The smaller the monitor, the bigger the case was. [laughs]

145
00:07:15,472 --> 00:07:17,712
- Back then, the cases were huge and the monitors looked like old TVs.
- Yes, true.

146
00:07:19,432 --> 00:07:22,352
And we had webcams too.

147
00:07:22,352 --> 00:07:23,632
In the internet cafe, there were only two sounds:

148
00:07:24,312 --> 00:07:24,632
laughing and cursing, and the typing sounds of older kids playing Audition.

149
00:07:25,852 --> 00:07:28,512
- Ah, clack-clack-clack-clack on the keyboards.
- It felt very cool.

150
00:07:28,512 --> 00:07:30,992
I could only play for about an hour before my dad picked me up. He wouldn't let me play more.

171
00:08:36,512 --> 00:08:37,912
My dad would always time it to pick me up for dinner.

172
00:08:38,592 --> 00:08:42,432
I'd play for only an hour at most, and then go home to eat dinner.

173
00:08:42,432 --> 00:08:43,472
At that time, leaving the Thanh Cong area,

174
00:08:44,412 --> 00:08:47,092
on weekends or whenever

175
00:08:47,952 --> 00:08:51,532
my grandparents were free, they would take me to Ho Thanh Cong

176
00:08:52,592 --> 00:08:53,552
to walk

177
00:08:54,332 --> 00:08:55,572
and practice riding a bicycle.

178
00:08:56,992 --> 00:08:57,352
Yeah.

179
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:01,472
Back then, the path around Ho Thanh Cong was always very

180
00:09:02,712 --> 00:09:03,892
rough and uneven.

181
00:09:04,792 --> 00:09:08,332
- It was completely different from now.
- It was concrete, not paved with stone like today.

182
00:09:08,332 --> 00:09:11,052
- Yes. And back then, you had to take the lower path.
- And the gate was very awkward.

183
00:09:14,532 --> 00:09:16,152
- You had to step over a high curb.
- Yeah.

185
00:09:16,152 --> 00:09:18,992
It always looked like it was blocked, as if they didn't want people to go in.

186
00:09:19,612 --> 00:09:21,412
- Yes, I remember that gate never opened fully.
- That's because we went through the back gate. The main gate was on the main street.

187
00:09:21,412 --> 00:09:26,052
- We never went through the main gate.
- No one from Thanh Cong ever went through the main gate.

188
00:09:26,052 --> 00:09:29,232
Exactly, locals always took the back gate because it was closer.

189
00:09:29,232 --> 00:09:32,132
- Yeah.
- And that back gate never opened fully for some reason. We had to squeeze in.

191
00:09:34,172 --> 00:09:37,812
- Squeeze our bicycles through.
- Squeeze the bicycle through, walk it down, and start riding.

192
00:09:37,812 --> 00:09:39,792
- You can't experience that now.
- Yeah.

193
00:09:39,792 --> 00:09:43,052
Because of the new policy, all park fences have been removed.

195
00:09:47,052 --> 00:09:50,952
- To make it open.
- But I don't understand why they had fences around parks in the first place.

196
00:09:50,952 --> 00:09:52,072
- Probably to keep out drug addicts. [laughs]
- Yeah, addicts.

197
00:09:52,292 --> 00:09:56,032
Right.

198
00:09:56,712 --> 00:09:59,402
What was your feeling when riding a bicycle around Ho Thanh Cong?

199
00:09:59,402 --> 00:10:00,912
- Riding a bicycle?
- Yes.

200
00:10:00,912 --> 00:10:03,171
To be honest, I didn't care about Ho Thanh Cong. Being forced to practice riding a bicycle made me hate it.

201
00:10:03,772 --> 00:10:04,472
Because if I play a sport for two minutes and don't immediately become good at it, I get upset.

202
00:10:06,572 --> 00:10:06,752
[laughs] Okay.

203
00:10:08,172 --> 00:10:11,732
I was terrified of riding a bicycle back then.

204
00:10:12,452 --> 00:10:13,412
I didn't like practicing in a place where people could see me fall.

205
00:10:13,412 --> 00:10:16,992
- Yeah.
- So I preferred practicing in the yard behind my grandmother's house.

206
00:10:16,992 --> 00:10:17,731
Also, around Ho Thanh Cong, there were many dogs, and sometimes

207
00:10:18,432 --> 00:10:19,112
there was a strong fishy smell because of dead fish floating around.

208
00:10:20,272 --> 00:10:24,452
- Ah, yes. Lately, I haven't seen dead fish anymore.
- Yes, the smell is fine now.

210
00:10:25,512 --> 00:10:28,972
- The ecosystem is better, or maybe there are no fish left.
- So when you think of Ho Thanh Cong, you remember the fishy smell,

211
00:10:30,812 --> 00:10:33,702
- unleashed dogs,
- and the fear of falling off the bicycle.

212
00:10:33,702 --> 00:10:35,752
- And you just wanted to go back to the internet cafe.
- Yes, heaven was always at home.

213
00:10:35,752 --> 00:10:37,432
- The internet cafe had air conditioning.
- While the school didn't.

214
00:10:37,432 --> 00:10:42,112
- Exactly.
- Okay, thank you.

227
00:10:42,908 --> 00:10:45,288
[background music]
